// D binding tests (extern(C) + link-time). Like Nim/Zig/Go-cgo/Rust, D compiles
// and links: the binding's own module (src/servirtium/package.d) is compiled
// into the test binary and the engine .so is linked with an rpath, so the test
// finds the engine at build time and at run time.
//
// tests/playback_test.d replays the canonical tape (GET /ok -> 200 text/plain
// "ok-body") and asserts the body, a clean match, the diagnostics, and what D
// adds (scope(exit) shutdown, GC'd strings with no manual free, a thrown
// VcrException instead of a dead handle).
//
// Deliberately driven through bash.test + tests/test_playback.sh rather than
// aeb's `d.test()` builder. d.test runs `dmd … -run <file> 2>&1 | tee <log>`,
// and a shell pipeline reports the status of its LAST command — so tee's 0
// masks both a dmd compile error and a failing test. That was observed here:
// this binding did not compile at all (an extern(C) function-pointer linkage
// error) and d.test still reported "1/1 PASS", with the real errors sitting in
// the tee'd log. bash.test runs `bash <script>` directly and propagates the
// exit code, so this suite can actually redden. (Same root cause as aeb's
// cpp.tests — see cpp/.tests.ae.) Revisit once aeb's d/cpp SDKs stop piping
// through tee.
//
// Skipped by preflight when dmd is absent (prereq dmd).
import bldr
import bash
import bash (script)
aeb(cap) {
    bldr.build() {
        prereq("dmd")
        dep("core/.build.ae")
        bash.test() {
            script("tests/test_playback.sh")
        }
    }
}
